 "final_message": "**Verdict: delivered and verified.** `render_dashboard(store, today=None)` in `taskboard/dashboard.py` returns one self-contained HTML page. All 31 tests pass, and independent QA passed every gate.\n\n**1. Class and roles.** Class C (rule `risk-signal`), because the dashboard is a new user-facing surface. Roles that ran:\n- design-lead wrote the spec.\n- senior-developer implemented it.\n- senior-frontend-engineer reviewed it.\n- QA verified it.\n- A UX advisor reviewed it.\n\nI skipped the business analyst, because your request already fixed the scope and acceptance criteria.\n\n**2. Files changed.**\n- `taskboard/dashboard.py` (new).\n- `tests/test_dashboard.py` (new, 21 tests).\n- `README.md` (one Layout bullet).\n- The store, db and reporting code are untouched.\n\n**3. Gates** (full table in `.oeo/20261030-html-dashboard-of-open-tasks-per-owner-w/verification.md`; `oeo verification-check` passes):\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| acceptance-criteria-defined | PASS |\n| business-review-passed | N/A: scope fixed by the user |\n| adr-recorded | N/A: no structural change |\n| diff-reviewed | PASS |\n| checks-pass | PASS |\n| regression-test | PASS |\n| domain-reviews-passed | PASS |\n| acceptance-criteria-met | PASS |\n| outcome-measurable | N/A: no deployed service to measure |\n\n**4. Acceptance criteria and evidence.**\n- **Self-contained page:** the output has no external CSS, JS, fonts, images or URLs, and `today` can be passed in.\n- **Counts per owner:** they come from the existing `open_task_counts`, and owners with no open tasks are omitted.\n- **Task lists:** done tasks are excluded. Tasks are sorted soonest-due first, with undated ones last and labelled \"No due date\".\n- **Overdue highlighting:** an overdue task gets a text \"Overdue\" badge, and each owner card shows an overdue count. A task due today is not flagged as overdue. QA confirmed that changing `<` to `<=` in the comparison fails two tests.\n- **Responsive and dark mode:** headless Chromium at 360px measured `scrollWidth` 360, equal to `clientWidth`, with a 120-character unbroken title. The page shows 4 columns at 1280px and switches in dark mode.\n- **Escaping and empty state:** an `<img onerror>` owner name and an `<svg onload>` title are both escaped. An empty store shows a \"No open tasks\" message.\n- **Tests and dependencies:** the new tests fail on the original code with `ModuleNotFoundError`. There are no new dependencies.\n- **Contrast:** every text pair is at least 7.35:1, and borders are at least 3.10:1. The ratios come from the repo's own test helper, not an independent tool.\n\n**5. Outcome.** A team lead can see who has how many open tasks and which are overdue. The UX advisor judged that outcome met, but flagged two gaps.\n- **Overloaded owners:** cards follow `open_task_counts` order, not load, so you compare counts by eye.\n- **Due next:** soonest-first sorting applies within each owner only, with no cross-owner view.\n\nI didn't build either, because they add scope. No user research backs them; they are the advisor's hypotheses.\n\n**6. Cost.** 109,275 subagent tokens against 180,000 planned and a 400,000 budget. QA and the senior developer ran over their per-agent estimates (see the cost table).\n\n**7. Open risks** (all minor, none blocking):\n- `today` passed as a string or datetime raises `TypeError`.\n- `date.fromisoformat` also accepts forms like `20261029`, which then render as dated tasks.\n- A malformed due date shows its raw text with no label. The design doesn't cover that case, and the behaviour is safe and tested.\n- `test_default_today_is_current_date` reads the wall clock, so it could flake at midnight.\n- `taskboard/__pycache__/` and `tests/__pycache__/` are untracked, with no `.gitignore` to hide them.\n\n**Next step (owner: you, as Business Owner).** Decide whether to add load-sorted cards or a cross-owner \"next due\" list. If you do, it runs as a new scope change. The minor fixes above can go in the same pass."
